WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.240
This story struck me personally

2
00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:06.020
because it has to do with Steven Spielberg.

3
00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:09.370
Some Oscar controversy is heating up around town.

4
00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:12.980
Deadline reports that the Oscars is cutting eight categories

5
00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:14.140
from the telecast.

6
00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:16.430
And Steven Spielberg is saying

7
00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:18.670
he hopes they'll change their mind.

8
00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:20.180 line:15%
The Academy plans to leave out

9
00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:23.270 line:15%
several short film categories, plus production design

10
00:00:23.270 --> 00:00:25.145 line:15%
which we are literally just talking about,

11
00:00:25.145 --> 00:00:26.780 line:15%
how important it is.
Yeah.

12
00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:29.470 line:15%
Original score music can change

13
00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:32.040 line:15%
the whole way you feel about a scene

14
00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:32.980 line:15%
you are watching.

15
00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:36.340 line:15%
Film editing which is a complete art in itself.

16
00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:39.120 line:15%
You choose the takes from the actors.

17
00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:42.040 line:15%
You choose what pieces of the story to leave in and out.

18
00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:44.980 line:15%
Oh, and makeup and hair styling, what?

19
00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:46.620 line:15%
What, yeah, I know.

20
00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:49.620 line:15%
They will give these awards out before the show

21
00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:54.270 line:15%
and edit their acceptance speeches into the live telecast.

22
00:00:54.270 --> 00:00:56.150 line:15%
Spielberg, and a chorus of critics

23
00:00:56.150 --> 00:00:59.590 line:15%
are saying these categories deserve to share the stage

24
00:00:59.590 --> 00:01:00.700 line:15%
alongside of them.

25
00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:02.607 line:15%
And Steven has been quoted saying,

26
00:01:02.607 --> 00:01:05.470 line:15%
"There is no above the line and below the line,

27
00:01:05.470 --> 00:01:09.060 line:15%
which means, stars and crew."

28
00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:10.820 line:15%
I totally agree with him.

29
00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:13.050
Steven has also said he is a complete fan

30
00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:14.530
of the president of the academy.

31
00:01:14.530 --> 00:01:16.790
This is also a network decision.

32
00:01:16.790 --> 00:01:19.340
And I think they're just trying to find a way

33
00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:22.410
to keep the pace alive,

34
00:01:22.410 --> 00:01:23.840
but at what cost?

35
00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:26.020
Exactly, we can't forget that movie making

36
00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:27.710
is such a collaborative process.

37
00:01:27.710 --> 00:01:30.070
As a fan, I want to see the people

38
00:01:30.070 --> 00:01:32.460
who make the movies being celebrated.

39
00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:33.580
That's the whole point.
Yes, yes!

40
00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:35.060
You have to put on a good show

41
00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:36.730
but you can't lose focus.
(audience cheers)

42
00:01:36.730 --> 00:01:37.970
Yeah.

43
00:01:37.970 --> 00:01:39.170
All right, next up,

44
00:01:39.170 --> 00:01:40.420
if there is a little leap

45
00:01:40.420 --> 00:01:42.050
that you're thinking of taking in your life,

46
00:01:42.050 --> 00:01:43.850
no matter how big or small,

47
00:01:43.850 --> 00:01:47.150
maybe this story will inspire you to just go for it.

48
00:01:47.150 --> 00:01:50.260
The Week reports, "It's about to be a huge homecoming

49
00:01:50.260 --> 00:01:51.670
for Tom Turcich.

50
00:01:51.670 --> 00:01:55.940
On April 2nd, 2015, a day before he turned 26

51
00:01:55.940 --> 00:01:59.290
Tom left his New Jersey home with one goal

52
00:01:59.290 --> 00:02:02.970
to travel the entire world on foot."

53
00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:07.570 line:15%
Yeah, "Since then he's traveled over 25,000 miles.

54
00:02:07.570 --> 00:02:09.840 line:15%
Most of it with Savannah right here,

55
00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:14.057 line:15%
a dog that he adopted on a stop in Texas," oh Savannah!

56
00:02:14.057 --> 00:02:18.340 line:15%
"And now Tom has burned through 45 pairs of sneakers

57
00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:21.220 line:15%
traveling to the mountains of Kurdistan

58
00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:23.660 line:15%
following a flock of sheep in Iceland,

59
00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:25.430 line:15%
kayaking through Antarctica.

60
00:02:25.430 --> 00:02:27.330
He was inspired to take this journey

61
00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:28.610
when he was just 17 years old

62
00:02:28.610 --> 00:02:30.580
because he lost a young friend

63
00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:34.210
and he realized that he wanted to make the most of the time

64
00:02:34.210 --> 00:02:35.900
we all have on this earth."

65
00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:37.536
And now, I mean, this story.

66
00:02:37.536 --> 00:02:39.860
(audience cheers)

67
00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:41.690
Now believe this or not.

68
00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:46.540
Now he is on day 1789 of his journey.

69
00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:50.430
He's just weeks away from making it home,

70
00:02:50.430 --> 00:02:54.920
walking around the entire world, what?

71
00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:56.960
And I just hope that he brought his Fitbit

72
00:02:56.960 --> 00:02:58.727
'cause can you imagine at the end you're like,

73
00:02:58.727 --> 00:03:03.310
"Oh, man, I didn't."
(Drew laughs)

74
00:03:03.310 --> 00:03:07.470
This story, it speaks to me so much

75
00:03:07.470 --> 00:03:10.248
that we have these choices in life.

76
00:03:10.248 --> 00:03:11.081
Yeah.

77
00:03:11.081 --> 00:03:13.490
And I have so much respect

78
00:03:13.490 --> 00:03:16.586
and admiration for his choices.

79
00:03:16.586 --> 00:03:19.169 line:15%
(upbeat music)

80
00:03:20.812 --> 00:03:22.899 line:15%
♪ Oh oh oh oh ♪

81
00:03:22.899 --> 00:03:24.740 line:15%
♪ Oh oh oh oh ♪

